@startuml interfaces
title Terminal — the interface catalogue

skinparam shadowing false
hide empty members
left to right direction

package "Utils::Terminal::Iface — opt-in mixins" #F8F8F8 {

  interface OnEvent {
    +callback : Callback
    +setCallback(Callback)
    +onEvent(Event&) <<virtual>>
  }
  note bottom of OnEvent
    The raw channel. A widget with no
    specific interface still sees every
    event through this one.
  end note

  interface OnHover {
    +isHovered : bool
    +onEnter : Callback
    +onLeave : Callback
    +setHovered(bool)
    #onHoverChanged(bool) <<virtual>>
  }

  interface OnClick {
    +isPressed : bool
    +onPress : Callback<MouseButton>
    +onRelease : Callback<MouseButton>
    +setPressed(bool, MouseButton)
    #onClicked(MouseButton) <<virtual>>
  }

  interface OnFocus {
    +hasFocus : bool
    +onFocusGained : Callback
    +onFocusLost : Callback
    +setFocus(bool)
    #onFocusChanged(bool) <<virtual>>
  }

  interface OnKey {
    +onChar : Callback<char>
    +onKey : Callback<EventType>
    #onKeyPressed(EventType) <<virtual>>
  }

  interface OnScroll {
    +onScroll : Callback<int>
    #onScrolled(int delta) <<virtual>>
  }

  interface OnDrag {
    +dragOrigin : Point
    +onDragStart : Callback<Point>
    +onDragMove : Callback<Point>
    +onDragEnd : Callback<Point>
    #onDragged(Point delta) <<virtual>>
  }
}

note as PATTERN
  **Every mixin has the same three parts**

  **state**     — what render() reads
  **callbacks** — compose: assign a lambda
  **hook**      — inherit: override it, protected
                  so it can't steal the callback

  Each setter calls invalidate() itself, so a
  hover change repaints with no widget code.
end note

OnHover .. PATTERN
OnClick .. PATTERN

@enduml
